{"paper": "2024-Tier1-26-Sep-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential-count-mismatch", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 24, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If the altitude from two vertices of a triangle to the opposite sides are equal, then the triangle will be:", "options": [{"text": "isosceles triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "equilateral triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "scalene triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "obtuse angle triangle", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A secant PAB is drawn from an external point P to the circle with the centre at O, intersecting it at A and B. If OP = 17 cm, PA = 12 cm and PB = 22.5 cm, then the radius of the circle is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "An article costs₹1,000 for a salesman. He fixes its marked price as₹1,500. He sells it to a customer at a discount of 20%. He gives a furtherdiscount of 10% for each cash payment. Find the percentage of loss or gain that the salesman makes on sale.", "options": [{"text": "gain 8%", "added": false}, {"text": "gain 10%", "added": false}, {"text": "loss 8%", "added": false}, {"text": "loss 10%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Simplify", "options": [{"text": "285", "added": false}, {"text": "224", "added": false}, {"text": "364", "added": false}, {"text": "310", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The monthly incomes of A, B and C are in the ratio 2 : 9 : 3 and their expenses are in the ratio 3 : 9 : 5. If A’s saving is half of his total income, then savings of A, B and C are, respectively, in the ratio of:", "options": [{"text": "3 : 9 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 5 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 18 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2 : 1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A tank is filled in 45 minutes by two pipes, A and B. Pipe B fills the tank twice as fast as A. How much time (in minutes) will pipe A alone take to fill the tank?", "options": [{"text": "135", "added": false}, {"text": "140", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "115", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "In a circular race of 1600 m in length, Bhaskar and Vinay start with speeds of 27 km/h and 45 km/h starting at the same time from the same point. When will they meet for the first time on the track when running in the opposite directions and the same direction, respectively?", "options": [{"text": "1 minute 20 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "1 minute 40 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "2 minutes 40 seconds and 5 minutes 40 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "2 minutes 20 seconds and 4 minutes 20 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "circular-track", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "66.09%", "added": false}, {"text": "76.09%", "added": false}, {"text": "76.07%", "added": false}, {"text": "66.07%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "In a triangle PQR, ∠ P + ∠ Q = 84°. Find the value of ∠ R.", "options": [{"text": "74°", "added": false}, {"text": "96°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "102°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Find the volume of a cone having base radius 3.5 cm and height 18 cm.", "options": [{"text": "241 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "221 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "201 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "231 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The following pie-chart shows the distribution of students at graduate level in different institutes in a town. Study the given chart and answer the question that follows. Distribution of students at graduate level institutes If the total number of students at the graduate level is 2,46,000, then how many students of institutes A and B are studying at graduate level?", "options": [{"text": "76,260", "added": false}, {"text": "74,580", "added": false}, {"text": "86,190", "added": false}, {"text": "78,370", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Ram’s income is 2.5% more than Shyam’s income. By what percentage is Shyam’s income less than Ram’s income?", "options": [{"text": "2.43%", "added": false}, {"text": "3.43%", "added": false}, {"text": "1.43%", "added": false}, {"text": "4.43%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "How much rice of ₹4 per kg should be mixed to 15 kg of rice of ₹10 per kg, so as to make a mixture worth ₹6.50 per kg?", "options": [{"text": "15 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "21 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "30 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "40 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "alligation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "54%", "added": false}, {"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "48%", "added": false}, {"text": "52%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "110", "added": false}, {"text": "130", "added": false}, {"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "8 years", "added": false}, {"text": "5 years", "added": false}, {"text": "4 years", "added": false}, {"text": "2 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A shopkeeper has a fault of 100 g in a 3 kg weight. He sold 3 kg of potatoes to Charu using the same faulty weight for ₹46. The cost price of the potatoes for the seller was ₹12 per kg. How much profit (in ₹) did he earn on the potatoes?", "options": [{"text": "11.6", "added": false}, {"text": "10.2", "added": false}, {"text": "11.2", "added": false}, {"text": "10 Q . 2 1 A 1. n s", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Find the value of the unknowns: x + 1.5y + 2z = 5.5 x + 5y + 7z = 15 3x + 11y + 13z = 25", "options": [{"text": "x = 2,y = -3,z = 4", "added": false}, {"text": "x = -3,y = 2,z = 4", "added": false}, {"text": "x = 4,y = -3,z = 2", "added": false}, {"text": "x = 2,y = 4,z = -3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Spoon", "added": false}, {"text": "Holder", "added": false}, {"text": "Plate", "added": false}, {"text": "Pipe", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}